[00:00] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Creator speaking with Netflix, Google Drive, and Spotify logos superimposed.
AUDIO: 'Sony recently announced that they\'ll be deleting movies from their PlayStation Store even if users previously purchased it. That\'s the moment I realized I don\'t actually own anything that I\'m paying for. So, I spent a week replacing the $1,000 I spend a year on subscriptions with things actually in my control. You'

[00:12] [scene:hardware]
VISUAL: A close-up shot of a Raspberry Pi board.
AUDIO: 'could do this too for less than the cost of 1 month you\'re already paying in subscriptions to watch Friends for the 50th time in a row. And the secret is this little baby right here. This is a Raspberry Pi. Now, don\'t be intimidated. I know it looks a little scary, but this'

[00:24] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'is basically just a mini computer that\'s super low power and perfect for running your own home server. So, you could either buy a Raspberry Pi or if you\'re cheap like me, don\'t want to fork any moolah over, any old laptop you have sitting at the bottom of your closet'

[00:36] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'will work, too. Don\'t worry about the specs unless you have one running off a hamster wheel, you\'ll be good. And the cost after that is basically only pennies of electricity to power it. Now, let me ask if you\'ve ever been in the same position as me. You\'re watching a show, it\'s your nightly comfort, you'

[00:49] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'can\'t wait to watch the next episode every night, and poof, it\'s gone from Netflix. It\'s on Pluto TV or Blingo or some other streaming service you\'ve never heard of. Are you really going to fork over another 15, 20 bucks a month to continue watching a show? Hell no.'

[01:01] [scene:talking head]
