AUDIO: 'files. But, something I\'ve heard about that I would never never ever do myself, there\'s many websites out there where you can acquire free movies, free TV shows, legally of course, and all above board. So, now you got your movies, now you got your shows, but that is just the'

[02:17] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera.
AUDIO: 'tip of the iceberg. These tech companies, their whole business model is to get you hooked for life on subscriptions. They want you to never cancel. And are you tired of letting Google host all your photos? These photos live on a server who knows where'

[02:29] [scene:meme]
VISUAL: A woman inside a large cage.
AUDIO: 'and are at the mercy of Google. There\'s stories of people getting banned for seemingly no reason. There goes all their documents, there goes their photos of their gam-gam\'s 90th birthday, everything. Are you really going to depend on a company who truly could not give two shits about you and the only'

[02:42] [scene:talking head]
VISUAL: Creator speaking to the camera with an animated graphic.
AUDIO: 'reason they support you is because they want to sell you ads? Are we really going to depend on them to keep our data safe? Well, I\'ve got another solution for you. There\'s a software out there, another open-source software called Image. This is a local Google Drive.'

[02:54] [scene:talking head]
